From 7f0b00b82bb6bec12ebbb9881a540ae90ac26d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kurtvan <kurtv7348@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:10:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blend an external texture into the feedback buffer

Adds projectm_set_feedback_texture/_mix/_luma_gate. Each frame, before the
warp pass, the active preset alpha-blends the caller's GL_TEXTURE_2D into
its previous-frame buffer (luma-gated), so the preset's warp distorts the
external image (e.g. live video) instead of it being overlaid.

Settings live on the ProjectM instance and are handed to whichever preset
is active, so they persist across preset loads. The blend program and VAO
are owned by the instance (FeedbackBlend), created on first use, with
uniform locations cached and blend/program/VAO/texture state restored.
